brief_summary:
In this study, the investigators want to find out whether drinking enough fluids works just as well and is as safe as receiving fluids through an IV during a sickle cell crisis. When patients are admitted to the hospital with a sickle cell crisis, they will receive one of two treatments: fluids through an IV, or encouragement and support to drink fluids. The investigators will compare the two groups to see whether there are differences in:

* how long patients need to stay in the hospital;
* how quickly patients can be discharged;
* how much pain patients experience;
* whether patients receiving IV fluids are more likely to retain too much fluid in the body, also called fluid overload.

The goal of the study is to better understand which way of giving fluids is most helpful and safest for patients during a sickle cell crisis.
